[vulkan] Use three swapchain images for FIFO on Android

Android's Vulkan loader sizes a swapchain's buffer queue to minImageCount - 1
plus the buffers its consumer holds (CreateSwapchainKHR in libvulkan's
swapchain.cpp), so the app can dequeue minImageCount - 1 buffers at once.
Dawn asks for two images in FIFO mode, so a frame can only start once the
compositor has given back the buffer shown before it. On Android 10,
SurfaceFlinger gives a SurfaceView's previous buffer back only after it has
composited the next one (BufferQueueLayer::releasePendingBuffer), and a
canvas presenting at the panel's rate waits for that in
vkAcquireNextImageKHR on every frame: 3.5 ms of each 16.7 ms frame on a
Mi MIX 3, with nothing else to draw.

Three images is the triple buffering Android gives every window it manages,
and what Khronos' mobile best practices ask for in FIFO mode.

Drop this patch when Dawn asks for three FIFO images on Android itself.

---
--- a/src/dawn/native/vulkan/SwapChainVk.cpp
+++ b/src/dawn/native/vulkan/SwapChainVk.cpp
@@ -73,6 +73,13 @@ uint32_t MinImageCountForPresentMode(VkPresentModeKHR mode) {
     switch (mode) {
         case VK_PRESENT_MODE_FIFO_KHR:
         case VK_PRESENT_MODE_FIFO_RELAXED_KHR:
+#if DAWN_PLATFORM_IS(ANDROID)
+            // Android's loader lets the app dequeue minImageCount - 1 buffers at once, so with two
+            // images each frame waits for the compositor to release the one shown before.
+            return 3;
+#else
+            return 2;
+#endif
         case VK_PRESENT_MODE_IMMEDIATE_KHR:
             return 2;
         case VK_PRESENT_MODE_MAILBOX_KHR:
